    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.indentscope\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI am using nvim-treesitter, in the simple config to reproduce the issue I added the tokyonight colorscheme, it is a colorful colorscheme so is easier to see that is happening.\n\nIf I set `vim.opt.wrap` to `true` the syntax highlighting works normally.\n\nHere is a video:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/89a17df7-d5a1-4126-adb0-aeff61e8ca7b\n\n### Reproduction\n\n\n```lua\nvim.opt.wrap = false\n\nlocal lazypath = vim.fn.stdpath 'data' .. '/lazy/lazy.nvim'\n\nif not (vim.uv or vim.loop).fs_stat(lazypath) then\n    local lazyrepo = 'https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git'\n    local out = vim.fn.system {\n        'git',\n        'clone',\n        '--filter=blob:none',\n        '--branch=stable',\n        lazyrepo,\n        lazypath,\n    }\n    if vim.v.shell_error ~= 0 then\n        vim.api.nvim_echo({\n            { 'Failed to clone lazy.nvim:\\n', 'ErrorMsg' },\n            { out, 'WarningMsg' },\n            { '\\nPress any key to exit...' },\n        }, true, {})\n        vim.fn.getchar()\n        os.exit(1)\n    end\nend\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\n\nvim.g.mapleader = ' '\nvim.g.maplocalleader = '\\\\'\n\nrequire('lazy').setup {\n    spec = {\n        {\n            'nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter',\n            lazy = false,\n            branch = 'main',\n            build = ':TSUpdate',\n        },\n        {\n            'folke/tokyonight.nvim',\n            lazy = false,\n            priority = 1000,\n            opts = {},\n        },\n        {\n            'nvim-mini/mini.indentscope',\n            version = false,\n            config = function()\n                require('mini.indentscope').setup()\n            end,\n        },\n    },\n    install = { colorscheme = { 'habamax' } },\n    checker = { enabled = false },\n}\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\n    pattern = { 'typescriptreact' },\n    callback = function()\n        vim.treesitter.start()\n    end,\n})\n\nvim.cmd [[colorscheme tokyonight]]\n\n```",
