        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I can reproduce the issue with this example code, move the cursor inside the `<button>Copy</button>` tag and the `onClick` function.\n\nUnfortunately, I can not (on `NVIM v0.12.0-dev-1159+g21f2c2b19c`, the latest available Neovim Nightly build). I used the provided repro setup, manually executed `:lua require('nvim-treesitter').install({ 'tsx' })`, and opened 'test.tsx' file with contents [from the comment](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/1986#issuecomment-3263328796). Navigating across all the file (*and* around both `onClick` words) has persistent highlighting.\n\n> I tested with Neovim v0.11.4 and it works fine, so it could be a problem with Neovim nightly as you say.\n\nI would be inclined to think so, yes. There were recently several significant changes that affected tree-sitter highlighting (neovim/neovim#31400). The ones that I encountered are resolved by neovim/neovim#35536. Are you comfortable with building Neovim from that PR and checking if *it* fixes the issue?\n\nIn the meantime I am going to close this. If you are not comfortable with checking with custom PR build, I'll try to reminder you when Nightly build has necessary changes.",
